# all-buttons.pad — every button one at a time, then the left stick to each extreme.
#
# For proving an input decode rather than for playing the game: the six buttons here are the ones the
# front end ignores, so the capture stays on one screen and nothing loads mid-run (a load stalls the
# game's tick counter, and a capture with a stalled tick is not replayable). Start and cross are
# deliberately absent for that reason, and select cannot be sent at all.
#
#   ./kit record watch/acceptance.toml --state 9 --pad watch/pads/all-buttons.pad -n 300
press l1 400
sleep 100
press r1 400
sleep 100
press l2 400
sleep 100
press r2 400
sleep 100
press triangle 400
sleep 100
press square 400
sleep 200
stick l -1 0
sleep 400
stick l 1 0
sleep 400
stick l 0 -1
sleep 400
stick l 0 1
sleep 400
stick l 0 0
release
